  "title": "AI in Indian Healthcare: Shift to Real-World Applications and Infrastructure",
  "summary": "Hospitals are using AI mainly for operational gains, but the next phase of adoption will require stronger digital infrastructure, workflow integration, and clinical oversight, while a report highlights that AI's potential in healthcare lies in remote monitoring, OT/ICU optimization, and post-discharge care. The report suggests that India's healthcare providers are shifting AI from experimental testing to real-world applications, driven by increased adoption rates and the need for improved value delivery.",
  "facts": [
